 "friction": [
  {
   "node": "S4.d1_t9",
   "issue": "Wrong answer (CT first in a child) is given as a 'hint' that never says the choice is wrong; I could not tell if I was wrong, so I just clicked Try again"
  },
  {
   "node": "S4.c2_t12",
   "issue": "Same hint-style wrong answer for scan before beta-hCG; the 'Tempting' lead-in reads as encouragement, not a correction"
  },
  {
   "node": "S1.age_a / S1.age_b / S2.age_probe",
   "issue": "The 'age decides the cause' rule is taught three times in S1-S2 with near-identical wording; for a fast clicker it is repetition, not new learning"
  },
  {
   "node": "S4.a2 / S4.a3 / S6.p6",
   "issue": "'A negative ultrasound does not exclude appendicitis in adults' is asked three times across segments 4 and 6 with the same answer; dead weight after the first"
  },
  {
   "node": "S4.a6 / S3.alv2 / S6.p3",
   "issue": "Alvarado scoring asked three times, and the S3 probe already gives the item weights; the S6.p3 case is nearly the same as S3.alv2"
  },
  {
   "node": "S5.p6",
   "issue": "Stem 'Which of these is NOT a complication of acute appendicitis itself, before any operation?' is a double negative; I had to re-read it and still guessed"
  },
  {
   "node": "S6.p2 / S5.p9",
   "issue": "Wrong-answer feedback often restates the correct answer in full ('Vomiting before the pain would have argued against appendicitis'), so the Try again loop is answered by reading, not thinking"
  },
  {
   "node": "S2.end_probe",
   "issue": "Correct answer stem and option wording are clear, but the 'Show me why' option is the only route to a teaching re-read and I never took it; guessers would reach the right answer with no teaching for the mechanism of the chain"
  },
  {
   "node": "S3.case_t1 / S3.rov_t1 / S3.obt_t1",
   "issue": "Movement-to-sign mapping is taught in S3.contrast before the probes, but the feedback text repeats 'Tempting' and 'Nudge' prefixes on every wrong answer, which felt like a template"
